Z||000002||Old Lar||07-24-2000||04:38 PM||||I started using <A HREF="http://www.zing.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.zing.com</A>  for posting my Fiero photos.  I initially tried Photopoint and couldn't get it to work. My short frustration index with computers kicked in and I figured out how zing worked..<P>I don't know how they make $$ when I just post photos.  I haven't got any coffee mugs, prints made or anything like that.  I use it to share my photos.||||reg||3
Z||000003||Robert||07-24-2000||10:09 PM||||I’ve been using WebShots    <A HREF="http://webshots.com" TARGET=_blank>http://webshots.com</A>    for some time now and am pleased with the service.  There is no cost or limit to the number of albums you can make.  I don’t know how they make their money, maybe it’s like most Internet Company’s, they don’t need to make money, they just need to see a lot of hits.  Someday they hope to do an IPO and cash out.<BR>I wouldn’t post any picture without keeping the original on my backup disk.  These companies might not be around tomorrow.  Nothing is forever….. I can remember buying my first “real” computer; an Apple IIe, and putting out the extra bucks for a second 360K disk drive, so I would “never” have to buy another computer again. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
